{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Where there are no oxen</b> — In this verse he warns to engage in the work of the soil." "<b>Oxen</b> — bulls. So too: ככבש אלוף (like a fatted lamb). That is, because there are no oxen the manger remains grain and clean, for there is nothing there. Another interpretation: where there are no bulls there is one manger of grain, in the sense of לשבור בר (to crush grain), and it is clean grain from the chaff." "<b>And abundant produce</b> — and many mangers filled with grain, by the strength of the bull, and this is sound:"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:39.368438576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}